+# Workflow world effects and Stop
+
+WorkflowEngine and its existing run/node journal own outcomes. The production workflow driver
+owns one cancellation scope for its world commands; the shared ExecutionPort owns their OS
+processes. No new task store, executor, permission authority or migration is introduced.
+
+```text
+world.run → running node → owned ExecutionPort command → result → same node receipt
+Stop → seal engine admission + abort owned commands → bounded receipt wait → run-settled
+```
+
+Do not close the shared ExecutionPort when one run stops. A Stop waits for that run's world
+commands and their durable receipts before confirming cancellation. The driver bounds cleanup to
+the Host's 1.5-second late-effect grace;
+an unresponsive command settles the run as interrupted with an explicit unknown-outcome error,
+and the Stop caller receives that error rather than a successful cancellation receipt.
+
+A completed command result arriving during or after Stop still updates its original journal
+node. It never releases a new descendant or emits progress after run-settled. A terminated command
+may have partial effects: its node retains an Interrupted uncertainty barrier rather than being
+made retryable. Cold resume/amend must not repeat it. Known completed results retain existing
+same-run replay and amended-cache invalidation semantics.
+
+The DSL permits an un-awaited world.run. Returning from the script with such an uncertain
+command cannot publish a completed run; it reports interruption. A script failure remains a
+failure, with any interrupted command's uncertainty retained in its original node.
+
+The run and node identities, desktop continuous events and remote replay source stay unchanged.
+Acceptance uses compiled workflow scripts, the production driver, real local commands and SQLite:
+Stop prevents a delayed write while another run on the shared executor completes; late completion
+is retained; non-cooperative cancellation is bounded and remains unknown; cold reopen cannot
+repeat an uncertain effect. Model transport and paid services are unnecessary for these cases.
